ADVERTISEMENT\par
\par
\par
The first idea of this Romance was suggested by the story of the\par
_Santon Barsisa_, related in The Guardian.—The _Bleeding Nun_ is a\par
tradition still credited in many parts of Germany; and I have been told\par
that the ruins of the Castle of _Lauenstein_, which She is supposed to\par
haunt, may yet be seen upon the borders of _Thuringia.—The Water-King_,\par
from the third to the twelfth stanza, is the fragment of an original\par
Danish Ballad—And _Belerma and Durandarte_ is translated from some\par
stanzas to be found in a collection of old Spanish poetry, which\par
contains also the popular song of _Gayferos and Melesindra_, mentioned\par
in Don Quixote.—I have now made a full avowal of all the plagiarisms of\par
which I am aware myself; but I doubt not, many more may be found, of\par
which I am at present totally unconscious.\par
\par
